            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/async/fdio.hpp",
                    "line": 97,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Should we terminate if timedOut==true here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/async/fdio.hpp",
                    "line": 97,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Reverted the API to old signature so no bool will be passed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/async/fdio.hpp",
                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why did we add this if it does nothing?  That seems like we could potentially end up dropping a missed error?   Go ahead and call `set_error` here so we don't miss this in the future."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/async/fdio.hpp",
                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure, i have added it in latest patch and now since we are returning an exception we don't need a new API for timed fdio as code became exactly same after i dropped the bool return."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/async/fdio.hpp",
                    "line": 153,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't really like that we have a timeout as a bool but we also now have a `set_error` for certain exceptions.  Can we treat a timeout as an exception and `set_error` in that case also?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/async/fdio.hpp",
                    "line": 153,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure, changed the code to return an exception in case of timeout. I also updated code to use same next() API rather than an extra new API as code became exactly same for both senders receiver pairs after dropping the return type bool."
                }
            ],
